WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:03.310
Get running, get running

3
00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:06.420
holding our flag high in the sky

4
00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:18.010
Cross this endless sea with me and search for

5
00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:21.770
a global miracle no one

6
00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:23.890
has yet been able to find

7
00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:27.920
With our hearts pounding,

8
00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:29.710
we'll just charge ahead as we please, following

9
00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:35.570
the footprints of those who pursue their dreams

10
00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:39.390
No matter how stormy the night,

11
00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:42.350
if we put our minds together,

12
00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:46.480
we'll get through it

13
00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:47.860
always

14
00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:51.550
Get running, get running

15
00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:54.490
holding our flag high in the sky

16
00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:57.090
Even though there are tears

17
00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:00.560
we don't want anyone to see

18
00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:03.450
Keep chasing, keep chasing

19
00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:06.460
the compass that leads to our dreams

20
00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:09.190
always points straight ahead

21
00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:11.340
We can't stop here

22
00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:21.450
Get running, get running,

23
00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:24.500
head past everyone else

24
00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:27.080
So long as we don't run from it,

25
00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:30.520
we can take hold of tomorrow

26
00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:33.550
Keep chasing, keep chasing

27
00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:36.470
everything we see in the moment,

28
00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:38.930
we should record it all

29
00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:41.390
the blank slates of our minds

30
00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:56.440
<b>Vital Response</b>

31
00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:13.680
Oh, Franky, I want to tell you something while we have a chance.

32
00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:14.690
Hm?

33
00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:21.320
Then, we can't do anything until we find that No. 2 key?!

34
00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:23.240
Yeah. That's right.

35
00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:25.490
How stupid!

36
00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:28.460
Well, at least I know what's going on.

37
00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:39.600
I'm really angry now!

38
00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:46.470
He sure is tough. He's up now.

39
00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:48.350
Stay there and watch.

40
00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:52.800
Franky...

41
00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:57.180
Destroyer Cannon!

42
00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:58.180
Wow!

43
00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:02.000
Ow, ow, ow! I don't like this attack
because it dislocates my joints!

44
00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.990
What?! You shouldn't do it, then!

45
00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:06.990
What a moron.

46
00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:12.540
I'm a Six Powers master.
Cannonballs would never hit me!

47
00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:15.040
No matter how much you run around,

48
00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:20.550
you can't escape from my
Franky Destroyer Cannon...

49
00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:24.550
because it's got homing cannonballs!

50
00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:27.310
Homing cannonballs?!

51
00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:31.810
Could it be that the cannonballs
sense the enemy and follow them?!

52
00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:45.320
I've never heard of such technology!

53
00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:47.280
What the heck is he?

54
00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:52.120
Huh?

55
00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:55.250
Hold it!

56
00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:57.670
So it's you who homes in on the enemy?!

57
00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:00.130
You jerk! Hold it!

58
00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:05.800
I fell for it! That bastard!

59
00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:14.540
He disappeared again.

60
00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:18.980
Where are you hiding?!

61
00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:21.700
It's no use searching for me.

62
00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:25.360
I'm an expert at Shave, one of the Six Powers.

63
00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:28.370
In addition to my lightning speed,

64
00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:33.830
I make no noise when moving about,
just like owls when they hunt.

65
00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:37.580
I execute perfect assassinations.

66
00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:44.010
An owl, huh?

67
00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:50.060
My target won't see me until
the very moment I kill him.

68
00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:51.020
Take this!

69
00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:54.310
He was hiding here.

70
00:04:56.270 --> 00:05:00.070
Looks like that attack caught
you completely off guard, huh?

71
00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:01.820
How impertinent!

72
00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:04.720
I've never experienced such humiliation!

73
00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:07.070
I'm a CP9 assassin!

74
00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:09.670
Shave!

75
00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:13.120
Whoa!

76
00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:17.380
Iron Ball!

77
00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:23.630
Ah! Watch out!

78
00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:27.090
Dammit! We're above the sea!

79
00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:34.770
Franky!

80
00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:40.400
This is terrible!

81
00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:44.440
If he gets swept away...

82
00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:46.780
he'll be headed straight
to the basin of the waterfall!

83
00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:49.780
Since he's in the sea, I can't rescue him.

84
00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:54.700
Franky! Hang in there!

85
00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:02.420
I can use Moon Walk if I get pulled into the waterfall.

86
00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:05.920
This is bad! I can't get out of the undertow!

87
00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:09.260
What a strong current! I can't
keep holding my breath, either!

88
00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:11.560
I have to get to the surface, no matter what!

89
00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:14.760
Sink deeper!

90
00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:20.880
That voice! Don't tell me
he broke the fridge door!

91
00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:29.220
What a feast!

92
00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:31.320
Hold on! He got fatter!

93
00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:35.790
Just how much food in that fridge did you eat?!

94
00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:48.960
I don't wanna drown in a place like this!

95
00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:52.930
Ahhh! I'm almost at the basin of the falls!

96
00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:56.390
I'll die! I'll die! I'm falling! Ahhh!

97
00:06:57.310 --> 00:06:59.770
Franky Butterfly!

98
00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:06.690
I won't let you get away!

99
00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:07.990
Moon Walk!

100
00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:16.980
Tough Dugong!

101
00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:24.130
That bastard!

102
00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:35.100
Weapons Left!

103
00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:36.220
Paper Art!

104
00:07:39.340 --> 00:07:40.230
Slime!

105
00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:46.020
Dammit! What the hell was that?!

106
00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:49.940
Oh, so close!

107
00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:53.450
This is really bad.

108
00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:55.120
I've just gotta get to the shore!

109
00:07:55.120 --> 00:08:00.080
1.0 Cola Cannon! Coup de Boo!

110
00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:06.290
Have you learned your lesson?

111
00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:09.130
It takes more than just strength
to defeat a Six Powers master!

112
00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:11.100
Strong Hammer!

113
00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:11.960
Paper Art.

114
00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:18.680
Fall into the falls!

115
00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:21.730
Strong Right!

116
00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:23.730
What?

117
00:08:24.430 --> 00:08:25.690
What?!

118
00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:28.640
Come with me!

119
00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:45.670
Let go of me, you bastard!

120
00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:49.670
Moon Walk with just one leg
can't support two people!

121
00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:53.010
We're gonna fall!

122
00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:55.510
Yeah, seems like it.

123
00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:59.760
So why don't you bring both of us
back to the shore before we fall?

124
00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:07.270
Or do you wanna try fighting me
while supporting our weight?

125
00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:09.190
I might win,

126
00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:12.190
but my life would be in danger, too.

127
00:09:13.190 --> 00:09:18.160
We're certainly in the same boat.
Take us back to the shore.

128
00:09:21.980 --> 00:09:24.080
Okay! That's right!

129
00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:25.580
Good job, good job.

130
00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:28.580
Let's get back to the shore together.

131
00:09:29.850 --> 00:09:33.690
But it looks like I'll win the fight once we get there!

132
00:09:33.690 --> 00:09:36.090
Oh? You think so?

133
00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:45.060
Yeah, because I just thought of a way
to finish you off with just one blow.

134
00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:49.480
Oh? So did I, Fukuro-kun.

135
00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:54.990
Now, what're you gonna do?

136
00:09:54.990 --> 00:10:00.200
Take me to the shore already
so that I can knock you out!

137
00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:06.960
You don't have to tell me!
I'll shut you up right here, right now!

138
00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:12.470
Super Cartwheel Iron Ball!

139
00:10:12.470 --> 00:10:15.630
I'll slam you into the corner of
the tower using this momentum!

140
00:10:17.900 --> 00:10:22.100
I see. It indeed looks like
I'll get smashed into pieces.

141
00:10:22.550 --> 00:10:25.560
Franky Centaur!

142
00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:30.810
I've got both your legs!

143
00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:34.320
Now you can't move however you want in the air!

144
00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:39.860
So what?! That still can't stop this momentum!

145
00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:41.870
That's not totally true.

146
00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:49.580
70mm 0.2 Cola Cannon!
A bit of Coup de Vent!

147
00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:53.240
Ahh! I lost my momentum!

148
00:10:53.240 --> 00:10:57.110
You stopped the cartwheel! Damn you!

149
00:10:57.110 --> 00:11:00.840
But this is enough!
We're already above the shore!

150
00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:02.840
Now, take this!

151
00:11:02.840 --> 00:11:06.750
70mm 1.5 Max Cola Power!

152
00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:08.110
Coup de...

153
00:11:08.110 --> 00:11:10.770
What're you doing?!

154
00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:17.940
Give up already, you bastard!

155
00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:19.070
Coup de...

156
00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:20.740
Vent!

157
00:11:28.480 --> 00:11:33.000
Super!

158
00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:43.440
Isn't the No. 2 key here yet?

159
00:11:43.440 --> 00:11:45.640
Zoro-kun! This is it for me! I'm exhausted.

160
00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:47.100
Carry me on your back.

161
00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:48.300
Why would I?!

162
00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:50.640
Tempest Kick.

163
00:11:58.230 --> 00:11:59.690
Finger Pistol!

164
00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:01.110
What're you doing?!

165
00:12:01.110 --> 00:12:06.070
You just aimed at me while pretending
to attack those two, didn't you?!

166
00:12:06.070 --> 00:12:09.080
That's a false accusation,
but if you want, we can fight.

167
00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:12.710
I've been frustrated for a while now
that you've been in my way.

168
00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:16.670
What'd you say?! That's what I
wanna say, you stupid herbivore!

169
00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:20.170
No, I'd have to say I prefer meat.

170
00:12:20.570 --> 00:12:22.970
We'll play rock-paper-scissors, Sogeking.

171
00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:25.770
– What?
– The problem is these handcuffs.

172
00:12:25.770 --> 00:12:28.310
There's a way to get them off of us.

173
00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:31.730
I'll cut off the hand of the loser.

174
00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:37.290
Wh-What's with you coming up with
such a scary idea looking so serious?!

175
00:12:37.290 --> 00:12:40.090
I'm not done! Keep listening!

176
00:12:40.090 --> 00:12:42.690
So the one who gets the handcuffs off like that...

177
00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:46.200
will hurry to Chopper with their cut-off hand...

178
00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:49.200
and have Chopper reconnect it to their wrist!

179
00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:51.660
We're not stuffed animals! Don't be ridiculous!

180
00:12:56.430 --> 00:12:58.430
I've got another idea.

181
00:12:58.430 --> 00:13:00.630
Ahh! Ahh! I don't wanna hear it!

182
00:13:02.990 --> 00:13:05.180
I'm tired of arguing.

183
00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:10.640
I can start anytime. The winner can
keep the prey all to himself.

184
00:13:18.190 --> 00:13:20.150
– Hm?
– What's that?

185
00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:35.620
Listen, Sogeking. Don't lose your posture.

186
00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:38.830
You are a sword!

187
00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:44.130
Someone get me a lawyer! I'll sue you for sure!

188
00:13:57.020 --> 00:14:00.120
I've never seen anyone with
as little self-discipline as him.

189
00:14:00.120 --> 00:14:02.720
I can't believe he gained that much weight in just a few minutes alone.

190
00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:12.740
You don't... need to be...
need to be... need to be...

191
00:14:12.740 --> 00:14:16.650
I'm not concerned! Just speak normally!

192
00:14:16.650 --> 00:14:18.040
That's “need to be concerned”, right?!

193
00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:19.540
Thank you!

194
00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:24.050
That's exactly what I was... I was... I was...

195
00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:26.350
I got it, so you can cut that out!

196
00:14:26.350 --> 00:14:28.550
Anyway, there's no need
to be concerned, then?

197
00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:30.050
Come back here!

198
00:14:30.050 --> 00:14:34.060
I was... I was... That's right!

199
00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:37.100
As for why,

200
00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:38.900
just watch!

201
00:14:38.900 --> 00:14:41.440
Vital Response!

202
00:14:44.140 --> 00:14:46.020
Wh-What the heck?!

203
00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:47.530
Digest!

204
00:14:48.790 --> 00:14:50.490
Absorb!

205
00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:52.490
Now, I'm back to normal!

206
00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:56.870
Ahhh! What?! What are you?!

207
00:14:56.870 --> 00:14:58.370
What did you just do?!

208
00:14:58.370 --> 00:15:00.250
Do it again.

209
00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:02.750
Vital Response!

210
00:15:02.750 --> 00:15:04.540
Digest!

211
00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:07.050
Absorb!

212
00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:13.180
You're amazing! How does that work?!

213
00:15:13.880 --> 00:15:17.600
Glad you asked!

214
00:15:18.180 --> 00:15:21.310
A thousand years at sea, and a
thousand years in the mountains...

215
00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:24.270
Breathing in the wind and drinking dewdrops,

216
00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:27.230
I trained myself, living as a hermit!

217
00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:33.740
After all that, I've... I've... I've...
I've acquired this “Vital Response”!

218
00:15:34.900 --> 00:15:39.120
Essentially, if you extend
your consciousness everywhere,

219
00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:45.130
from your hair to your internal organs,
toes, even the tip of your downy hair,

220
00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:50.220
there's no part of your body
that you can't manipulate.

221
00:15:51.020 --> 00:15:54.080
Extending your consciousness
even to the tip of your hair?

222
00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:57.600
I've read about that kind
of ability in a book before.

223
00:15:57.600 --> 00:15:59.600
It's called something like biofeedback.

224
00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:04.940
Then your hair moves around like
an octopus because of that ability?!

225
00:16:07.650 --> 00:16:10.900
An octopus?! How terribly rude!

226
00:16:11.500 --> 00:16:15.240
Call me... a valiant...

227
00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:24.000
lion... will... will you?!

228
00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:26.500
Why does it matter which one?

229
00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:29.920
Vital Response!

230
00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:31.520
Hair Bind!

231
00:16:44.850 --> 00:16:45.850
Dammit!

232
00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:49.520
If those catch me, I'm done for!

233
00:16:49.520 --> 00:16:50.480
Shave!

234
00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:52.530
Where did he go?!

235
00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:59.200
Finger Pistol: Cue!

236
00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:06.170
That stick doesn't even have a pointed tip!

237
00:17:10.130 --> 00:17:11.760
Cue! Cue! Cue!

238
00:17:12.560 --> 00:17:14.170
Heavy Gong!

239
00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:15.010
Iron Body!

240
00:17:20.970 --> 00:17:23.430
Ow, ow, ow!

241
00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:26.190
What's the matter?!

242
00:17:26.190 --> 00:17:27.490
Dammit!

243
00:17:27.490 --> 00:17:32.110
As I thought, he won't budge unless
I attack with Arm Point or Horn Point.

244
00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:37.820
But rumble balls are potent drugs.

245
00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:40.330
The proper dosage is one every six hours.

246
00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:42.830
If I take more than that,
it'll be a huge strain on my body.

247
00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:47.620
Plus, the second one will
alter the transformation wavelength,

248
00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:51.130
and so it'll be hard to
control my transformations.

249
00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:55.720
With the third one, I'll lose consciousness
and hardly be able to fight.

250
00:17:55.720 --> 00:17:59.890
What do I do? I could get stronger if I just take one more.

251
00:18:02.390 --> 00:18:06.890
I'll roast you on a skewer!

252
00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:10.890
Shishi Kebab!

253
00:18:25.910 --> 00:18:28.410
I'm just wasting time like this!

254
00:18:28.410 --> 00:18:29.540
Rumble!

255
00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:33.200
The risk is high, but I have a chance!

256
00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:35.210
It's now all or nothing!

257
00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:38.220
I'll somehow finish this within three minutes!

258
00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:39.200
Take this!

259
00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:40.540
Horn Point!

260
00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:41.890
What?!

261
00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:44.470
Wrong one!

262
00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:46.220
Ow, ow, ow!

263
00:18:47.680 --> 00:18:49.100
Kebab!

264
00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:52.690
Jumping Point!

265
00:18:53.540 --> 00:18:55.650
Ah! Wrong one!

266
00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:15.550
As I feared, I can't control
my transformations. Dammit!

267
00:19:15.550 --> 00:19:17.760
If only I could somehow use Arm Point,

268
00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:21.280
I could hit him with a full-powered Cloven attack!

269
00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:24.260
The fire is spreading, making this room more dangerous.

270
00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:29.220
This is no time for me to be stuck
with a guy with no key on him!

271
00:19:29.220 --> 00:19:33.690
I'd better hurry up and get the No. 2 key...

272
00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:36.980
and free Zoro and Sogeking!

273
00:19:36.980 --> 00:19:40.700
Or we can't rescue Robin!

274
00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:45.380
That's right! Robin!

275
00:19:45.380 --> 00:19:48.330
That's right! I'm...

276
00:19:49.030 --> 00:19:50.290
I'm...

277
00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:55.880
I'm fighting in order to save our friend!

278
00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:58.980
What a tough animal!

279
00:19:59.960 --> 00:20:02.930
Vital Response!

280
00:20:12.570 --> 00:20:14.770
His hair took the form of hands!

281
00:20:14.770 --> 00:20:18.480
I have to do it! I can't be
defeated in a place like this!

282
00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:20.900
I'm their only hope!

283
00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:23.110
Shishi Finger Pistol!
